
# CRDT Collaborative Editor

A real-time collaborative text editor built with [Yjs](https://yjs.dev/),
[Quill](https://quilljs.com/), [FastAPI](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/), and
PostgreSQL. Changes are synchronized over WebSockets and persisted as Yjs
updates, so document state survives server restarts.

## Features

- Real-time collaborative editing
- Shared Quill rich-text content
- Remote cursor support
- PostgreSQL-backed Yjs update storage
- Persistent document state
- REST endpoint for listing stored documents
- Configurable backend origin and frontend backend URL

## Project structure

```text
.
├── backend/
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── main.py       # FastAPI app, WebSocket and REST routes
│   │   ├── database.py   # Async SQLModel/PostgreSQL connection
│   │   ├── models.py     # Stored Yjs update model
│   │   ├── schemas.py    # API response schemas
│   │   ├── store.py      # PostgreSQL Yjs store
│   │   └── config.py     # Environment-based settings
│   └── pyproject.toml
└── frontend/
    ├── src/main.js       # Yjs, Quill and WebSocket setup
    ├── index.html
    └── package.json
```

## Requirements

- Python 3.14
- PostgreSQL
- Node.js and npm
- [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) for Python dependency management

## Configuration

Create the environment files from the provided examples:

```bash
cp backend/.env-example backend/.env
cp frontend/.env-example frontend/.env
```

Configure PostgreSQL in `backend/.env`:

```dotenv
POSTGRES_SERVER=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_DB=doc
POSTGRES_USER=your_postgres_user
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=your_postgres_password
```

The optional `ORIGINS` setting controls the FastAPI CORS allow-list. If it is
not set, all origins are allowed.

Configure the frontend server URL in `frontend/.env`:

```dotenv
VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

For an HTTPS backend, use `https://...`; the frontend converts this to a
`wss://` WebSocket URL. HTTP URLs are converted to `ws://`.

## Run locally

Start PostgreSQL and make sure the database named in `POSTGRES_DB` exists.

In the first terminal, start the backend:

```bash
cd backend
uv sync
uv run fastapi dev app/main.py
```

The API runs at `http://127.0.0.1:8000` by default.

In a second terminal, start the frontend:

```bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open the Vite URL printed in the terminal, normally
`http://localhost:5173`.

To edit or open a specific document, add a document ID to the URL, for example:

```text
http://localhost:5173/my-document
```

Browsers using the same URL share the same Yjs room. Without a document ID,
the frontend uses `default-document`.

## API

### WebSocket

```text
ws://127.0.0.1:8000/ws/documents/{doc_id}
```

The WebSocket endpoint receives Yjs updates for the document and loads or
stores updates through the PostgreSQL Yjs store.

### List documents

```http
GET /documents/
```

Example response:

```json
[
  {
    "path": "my-document"
  }
]
```

Interactive API documentation is available at:

- Swagger UI: `http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs`
- OpenAPI JSON: `http://127.0.0.1:8000/openapi.json`

## Build

Build the frontend production bundle:

```bash
cd frontend
npm run build
```

The output is written to `frontend/dist/`.
